  "_doc_disabled_timer_exempt": "Unit names the disabled-timer check must NOT report — timers deliberately left off. A distinct axis from `classes` above: that one keys on remediation CLASS names and gates privileged sudo action, this one keys on UNIT names and gates only a report, never an action. Empty by default, so every installed .timer whose UnitFileState is `disabled` while its vendor preset says `enabled` is reported as drift. FILLED 2026-10-26: Larry idled the autonomous factory (\"turn it all off\"): 82 timers and 8 daemons disabled that evening on top of the 16 disabled 2026-09-16, keeping only the RSDPM product chain (ourliberty-rsdpm-*), heal-rsdpm-install-drift, sync, system-resource-watch, larry-alerts-retention, agent-core-health, ci-runner-watchdog and the Beacon bot (the Telegram pipe). Every unit below is OFF ON PURPOSE; the list is the record (~/agents/state/factory-off-2026-10-26.txt on the droplet has the same names). Bring one back with `sudo systemctl enable --now <unit>` and remove it from this list.",
